Z||000000||Zoom88||10-31-2001||11:30 PM||||  I have been trying to get some info. on my car from several different sites but I get allot of conflicting information. Can anyone give me reliable info. ? I have a 1988 Formula, v6, 5 speed I would like to know what transmission it has or where I look to find out, as well 1st,2nd,3rd,4th,& 5 gear ratios. Also my car came stock with 15X6 Front Rims and 15X7 Rear, I would like to know what the offset the rims have.<P> Any info. would greatly be appreciate !!!<BR>I just found some tires I am going to try for the rear, I have always been partial to Dunlop specially that D60 A2, in my opinion one of the best tires you can buy for the money. But this time I am going with the Dunlop SP Sport 8000, 245/50ZR15 SL for the rear, Seems to be a good package, Z rating, Rim width range is 6.5-9.5" , Meas. rim width 7" , Thread width 9.1", overall dia. 24.7. <P>Diameter Ratio compared to the original (215/60-15 rear)is 98%, speedometer difference at 70 mph is + 1.5 MPH (or 71.5 mph) Clearances :Tire thread (around outside)-0.26", Tire Outside 0.59", Tire Inside 0.59" (this was calculated using a 42mm offset for the rear, would us the correct one if I knew what it was !!!)   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>Is anyone currently running this size and brand on the rear of stock 15X7 rims ?<P><BR> Thanks and for those of you who haven't seen it yet....my car is viewable on my website <A HREF="http://www.diginostics.com" TARGET=_blank>www.diginostics.com</A>  ....If anyone would like me to post pictures of thier car on my site I will glad to do it, just add any info you would like me to add along with the picture (optional). <P> -=ZRRRrroooOMM 88=- 8~)<BR><p>[This message has been edited by Zoom88 (edited 10-31-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000001||Formula88||11-01-2001||09:16 AM||||Well, your Formula has the Munci/Getrag 5-speed (Getrag 282).  I don't know the ratios, but I'm sure someone will post them.  I'm also quite sure a lot of people are going to tell you 245/50's are too big for your rims, even though they perfectly match the rim specs provided by the tire manufacturer.  I'm not sure on that one.  Many people were telling me it was too wide when I mentioned using those very same tires on my Formula.  I ended up going with Bridgestone RE950's in the stock sizes.  Not sure if I should have gone with the SP8000's anyway.  There are people on here who are successfully running 245/50-15's on the rear of a Fiero.  The detractors will say you are sacrificing some handling by going to an oversize tire.  I can't confirm that - but it's something to consider.  Check out the responses I got when I asked this question.  It might help.<BR> <A HREF="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum1/HTML/008916.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum1/HTML/008916.html</A> <P>If you decide to go with the SP8000's, let me know how you like them!  I'm curious as to how they'll do.  Good Luck!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||14
Z||000002||Zoom88||11-02-2001||08:40 AM||||Anybody? Still looking for info on rim offset and tranny gear ratios .......<P>Thanks Formula88 for the info. I will let you know about the tires.<P>||||reg||5
Z||000003||DRH||11-02-2001||09:04 AM||||Look here for the tranny ratios (all models):<BR> <A HREF="http://www.mindspring.com/~fierosketch/osg/tranny.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.mindspring.com/~fierosketch/osg/tranny.html</A> <P>The same site lists the 88 offsets as 41mm rear, 37 front.<P>There is a <B>ton</B> of useful info on that site, here's the main page:<BR> <A HREF="http://www.mindspring.com/~fierosketch/osg/" TARGET=_blank>http://www.mindspring.com/~fierosketch/osg/</A> <P>||||reg||1
